# {{PRODUCT}} — Gemini CLI / Antigravity

Follow `AGENTS.md` and `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md`; the kernel wins.

- Python: `{{PY}}` | Assemble: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` | Device: {{DEVICE_POLICY}} | {{GIT_POLICY}}
- Phone E2E: `.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md` (unit tests cannot substitute). UI diagnostics: `.agents/workflows/android-ui.md` (`android-ui list/render`, `android-ui hub` after fresh install/start; advisory only).
- Harness Boundary: `.agents/**` is immutable and `.agents/scripts/**` is an implementation detail; execute documented commands directly without inspecting or patching `.agents/**`. On traceback or `INCIDENT_RECORDED=<id>`, ask via `ask_question` whether to submit the anonymous Zero-PII report once (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py report-issue --submit --incident-id <id>`), enable `--always-auto-submit`, or keep local.
- Discovery: Graph-backed (`{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` or `--symbol <name>`; for unknown/cross-module targets, `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py graph --feature <name> --json` or `--find <symbol>` first). Search never anchors initial discovery.
- Consultation & Pre-Planning Clarification:
  - Read-only inquiries strictly inspect and report in chat; never invoke `draft` or mutate files unless implementation is requested.
  - When asked to study, compare trade-offs, or surface edge cases before starting, discuss in plain chat BEFORE invoking `draft`.
  - Before `draft`, clarify missing requirements or hard decisions (Room schema, exported components, permissions, public contracts): ask the developer about it with `ask_question`; for a Room change ask about an existing destructive fallback, users on older schema versions and downgrade first. Carry answers into `--approach` / `--risks` / `--device-strategy` (resolve `PLAN_GAPS=` via `revise`).
- Plan Approval Clarity & Antigravity Planning Lifecycle:
  - The approval question is the request: never add a separate sentence asking for approval.
  - The interactive Proceed button appears ONLY on initial task plan approval. Never tell the developer to click 'Proceed' on follow-ups or bug fixes during active tasks; execute, compile, and deploy directly (if the developer modifies or drops an Outcome/Approach detail mid-task within approved file scope, record `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task plan-note --task-id <id> --text "<english refinement>" --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` before `prepare-verification`). When the developer approves in chat, immediately run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` (atomically transitions to `IMPLEMENTING`); never ask the developer to run shell commands manually.
- Unified Chat & Question UI/UX (Language-Adaptive):
  - Match the developer's active conversation language dynamically and use the 5 canonical Markdown layouts from `.agents/rules/harness-rules.md` (no emoji): Plan Approval Card, Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`), Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`), 3-Section Mobile Walkthrough, and Commit & Delivery Card.
  - Ask every DEVELOPER_ACTION with `ask_question` in self-contained markdown with bold labels: for Plan Approval, follow the `APPROVAL_QUESTION` line that `draft`/`revise` print (first `PLAN_DOCUMENT_URI` as a clickable markdown link to `plan.md`; then the `APPROVAL_BRIEF` lines translated, each said once, as markdown with bold labels, never in a code block; after revising an approved plan, ask only about the change; when the developer asked for the change, never ask first whether to revise); for Mobile Walkthrough, include the 3-section walkthrough with `| # | Action | Expected Result |`; for Commit & Delivery, include verified files and fenced `text` Conventional Commit block in chat and inside `ask_question`, and on "Committed - verify and deliver" run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task deliver --repo . --task-id <id>`; in a right-to-left language, start each line with a word in that language and put code names, file names, values and English terms in backticks.
- Operational Guardrails:
  - Cancel is the developer's: only when the developer asks in chat, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task cancel --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<their words>"`; never cancel on your own or undo file edits. Up to 3 disjoint tasks may coexist (`task switch --task-id <id>`).
  - Developer-written reasons: when a gate asks the developer to run a command with `--proof-reference`, keep the `"<why ...>"` placeholder; never write their reason for them.
  - Gate vs Developer Instruction: when a gate refuses something requested, stop and ask with `ask_question` quoting the gate message and options.
  - Deferred Translations: add base strings with `l10n-todo="true"`; never copy base text into another locale or mark user-facing text `translatable="false"`.
  - Durable Context & PM: clarify ambiguity then translate into English before `context note` / `context instruct`. Before any PM MCP mutation, preview exact changes and record approval via `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py pm authorize --proof-reference "<phrase>"` (never overwrite Bug descriptions or set `Done`/`Closed` without explicit order). Run `zoho start-sync` / `zoho delivery-sync` when linked; use `task heal --task-id <id> --prepare-fresh-run` on stale state.
  - Existing File Edit & Native Proof Boundary: use `edit_file` / `replace_file_content` for existing files (`write_file` only for new files). Never write Antigravity transcripts or `.system_generated` files.
- Next-Action Router, Zero-Polling & Strict Verification Order:
  - Follow `NEXT_ACTION` directly; query `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task status --task-id <id> --next --brief --json` only when missing. Never poll background tasks/subagents (`manage_task`, `manage_subagents`, `schedule`, or `.system_generated/tasks/*.log`).
  - Strict verification order: 1. preflight -> 2. unit tests -> 3. routed reviewers -> 4. assemble/device install -> 5. mobile walkthrough -> 6. verify. Wait for ALL routed reviewers to PASS before `assemble`/device. No self-certification (`record_review.py --verdict PASS` is forbidden on HIGH/CRITICAL or sensitive changes). False positives use `task validate-finding --status FALSE_POSITIVE --reason "<rationale>"`.
- Review Host Binding & Exact Reviewer Dispatch Procedure (Antigravity):
  - Prepare verification: `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` (`review_protocol_version = 2`).
  - On `DISPATCH_REVIEWERS` (or `DISPATCH_PHASE_REVIEWERS` after `phase-review package --task-id <id> --phase-id <phase>`):
    1. If `before_first_dispatch` (`SELECT_REVIEW_MODEL`) is present, ask via `ask_question` and run its `command_template` first.
    2. Invoke every reviewer in `reviewers` in parallel in the same turn via `invoke_subagent`: `TypeName = role`, `Role = role`, Prompt = `reviewer_prompts[role]` (one-line pointer; fallback to `review_execution_profile.reviewers[role].brief_content` only if pointer is absent), `Workspace = inherit`, and `Model = "flash"` if `reviewer_models[role]` starts with `gemini-3.8-flash-` else omit `Model` (`INHERIT_PARENT_BY_OMISSION`).
    3. If subagent not found, read `.agents/subagents/<role>.json`, call `define_subagent` (all write/subagent/MCP flags `false`), and re-invoke.
    4. Print the Reviewer Dispatch Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Status |`) and yield without polling.
    5. On completion, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` (or `phase-review complete`). On `WAIT_FOR_*_REVIEWERS`, output at most one short progress line (e.g. `1/3`). On `RETRY_*_REVIEW_PROTOCOL`, send the router's exact `send_message`. On `*_BLOCKED`, stop and report.
    6. Once all complete, run `review finalize --task <id>` (or `phase-review finalize` then `task begin-next-phase --task-id <id>`), and report the Review Verdict Table (`| Reviewer | Model | Verdict | Findings |`).
- Mobile Verification Walkthrough & Device Verification:
  - On `MOBILE_VALIDATION_DECISION`, run `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py device install-start` (or `device skip-validation --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`).
  - After install succeeds, print the 3-section Mobile Verification Walkthrough in chat AND in the SAME turn invoke `ask_question` for sign-off (`device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"`, or `e2e start --task-id <id>` per `.agents/workflows/phone-e2e.md`).

## Canonical Command Catalog & Sequential Lifecycle

| Step | Stage | Canonical Command | Notes |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| 1 | **Discovery** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task-context --file <path> --json` (or `--symbol <name>` / `graph --feature <name> --json`) | Graph-backed AST discovery |
| 2 | **Draft Plan** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task draft --repo . --task-id <id> --outcome "<outcome>" --kind <AUTO\|BUG\|FEATURE\|REFACTOR\|CONFLICT> --expected-files <paths>` | Create plan (`CONFLICT` for Git merge conflicts: never drop branch code silently; ask via `ask_question` on semantic conflicts) |
| 3 | **Approve Task** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task approve --repo . --task-id <id> --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>" --enforcement-tier RULE_ENFORCED --plan-hash <hash from PLAN_HASH>` | Record chat approval -> `IMPLEMENTING` (run `zoho start-sync` if linked) |
| 4 | **Compile / Gate** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py compile` -> `task prepare-verification --repo . --task-id <id> --host antigravity` -> `preflight` -> `test` | Or `verify-steps --task-id <id> --host antigravity` |
| 5 | **Reviews V2** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py review complete --task <id> --reviewer <role> --execution-id <convId>` -> `review finalize --task <id>` | Phase reviews use `phase-review package/complete/finalize`; `task validate-finding` for false positives; `task resume` for fixes |
| 6 | **Assemble & Device** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py assemble` -> `device install-start` -> `device signoff --task-id <id> --verdict PASS --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` | Or `device skip-validation` / `e2e start` |
| 7 | **Verify & Deliver** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py task verify --repo . --task-id <id>` -> `task complete` -> developer commit -> `task deliver` | Run `zoho delivery-sync` if linked |
| - | **Context** | `{{PY}} .agents/harness.py context note "<english-note>"` / `context instruct "<english-instruction>" --scope "<scope>" --source conversation --proof-reference "<phrase>"` | Supports `--replace`, `--remove`, `--supersedes` |
